 "eras": [
  {"id":"1733","year":"1733","label":"Bajirao at Rajpuri","short":"1733","lens":"none","summary":"Bajirao I camps at Rajpuri to reduce the island fort, which holds out behind its bastions and sea.","basis":"The 1733 campaign is from Dighe (1944), summarised in docs/research/janjira-1733.md. The drawn fort is the 1771 plan's outline, bastions and gates carried back 38 years, marked inferred.","conjecture":"No plan of 1733 was found. The plan of 1771 and the present OSM lines are carried back unchanged; the palace was built under Sidi Surul Khan after 1700 and the 1733 buildings are unknown.","sources":["JAN-03","JAN-04","JAN-19","JAN-18"],"facts":["Bajirao I established himself at Rajpuri in 1733 for operations against Janjira; the attack depended on Angre's fleet, which did not come (Dighe 1944, via the 1733 note).","Sambhaji tried to fill the channel to the mainland in 1682 (Wikipedia)."]},
  {"id":"1774","year":"1774","label":"Dalrymple's plan","short":"Siddi stronghold","lens":"engraving","summary":"The Siddi stronghold as drawn by A. Werner in 1771 and published by Dalrymple in 1774: 18 round bastions, two gates, two tanks, the palace, a mosque and the magazine on the hill.","basis":"The inset \"Gingerah Fort\" on the plan, registered to OSM by fitting the island outline only. The plan's palace, citadel and two tanks fall within 3-15 m of the OSM features, which were not used in the fit.","conjecture":"The plan is an engraving: positions are good to about 15 m, no heights are given, and about 80 small house blocks are not traced. The printed scale bar and the fitted scale differ by 24%; the fit is used. The sea approaches and soundings are not drawn.","sources":["JAN-03","JAN-04","JAN-06","JAN-19"],"facts":["The plan's legend: a. The Seddee's house, b. The mosque, c. Two tanks, d. A large magazine on the hill, e. The two gates.","The plan shows 18 bastions; Wikipedia and a travel page say 19.","Imprint reads June 1771, A. Dalrymple; the BnF records date the two copies 1774 and 1784."]},
  {"id":"today","year":"Today","label":"ASI monument","short":"Monument","lens":"none","summary":"A protected monument reached by boat from Rajapuri, with the ruined palace, two tanks and the bastioned wall.","basis":"The OSM wall line, tanks, palace and citadel, plus the bastions, gates, mosque and magazine traced from the 1771 plan.","conjecture":"The plan elements are 1771 positions with the registration error above; whether each survives is not checked. Heights are unknown (kerb-high) in this evidence layer; see the constructed layer. The 1860 fire burnt more than half the buildings.","sources":["JAN-03","JAN-04","JAN-19","JAN-21"],"facts":["A fire in 1860 burnt more than half the buildings in the fort and destroyed many state papers (hand level, Sohoni).","Only the OSM-mapped features are checked against today; the rest are plan positions."]}
 ],
